# REQ-015: Non-Functional Requirements

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Medium (testing & validation); High (scalability architecture)
**Risk:** Medium
**Depends On:** All functional requirements (REQ-001 to REQ-014)

---

## User Story

As a product owner and engineering team,
I need the system to meet defined performance, availability, scalability, accessibility, and compatibility targets,
So that the solution is safe, reliable, and usable across the full range of GP practice sizes and user devices.

---

## NFR-001: Performance

**Target:** p99 latency < 2 seconds for all user-facing interactions.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] 99% of all user-facing page loads and interactions complete in under 2 seconds, measured end-to-end from user action to UI response.
- [ ] This target applies across all functional areas: inbox load, document open, search, filing, coding, task creation, annotation.
- [ ] Performance is measured under realistic concurrent load (see NFR-003 Scalability).
- [ ] SLOs defined inline within individual REQ-*.md files are consistent with this overarching target and take precedence where more specific.

**Notes:**
- Document viewer first-render (REQ-004) and file conversion (REQ-005) have their own SLOs which may extend beyond 2 seconds for large files; these are explicitly carved out and documented in their respective requirements.

---

## NFR-002: Availability

**Target:** 99.9% uptime measured on a rolling 30-day basis.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] System availability ≥ 99.9% per calendar month (equivalent to ≤ 43.8 minutes downtime per month).
- [ ] Planned maintenance windows are excluded from availability calculation provided they are communicated to practices with appropriate notice.
- [ ] Partial degradation (e.g. a single inbound source unavailable per REQ-002) does not count as full system unavailability provided the core inbox and filing workflow remain functional.
- [ ] Availability is monitored continuously; alerts triggered before SLO breach.
- [ ] Recovery Time Objective (RTO): system restored within 1 hour of a full outage.
- [ ] Recovery Point Objective (RPO): no more than 15 minutes of data loss in a full outage scenario.

