## NFR-006: Security Baseline

> These are the platform-level security NFRs. Individual REQ-*.md files contain requirement-specific security checks.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] All HTTP traffic over TLS 1.2+ (SEC-001).
- [ ] `@emisgroup/acp-security-headers` included in all frontend package.json dependencies (WSEC-013).
- [ ] No secrets, credentials, or API keys in source code or environment variables — Azure Key Vault only (SEC-002).
- [ ] All user-supplied URL values encoded with `encodeURIComponent()` (WSEC-006a).
- [ ] Dependency vulnerability scanning run as part of CI pipeline; critical CVEs block deployment.

---

## NFR-007: Observability Baseline

> These are the platform-level observability NFRs. Individual REQ-*.md files contain requirement-specific OTEL spans and SLOs.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] All services instrumented with OpenTelemetry (OTEL); traces, metrics, and structured logs emitted.
- [ ] p99 latency dashboards configured for all user-facing operations.
- [ ] Availability monitoring configured; alerting triggers before 99.9% SLO breach.
- [ ] Error rate dashboards configured; anomalous error rates trigger alerts.
- [ ] All audit log writes monitored; failures trigger immediate alerts (see REQ-009).

