## Design (Added by V1c)

### API Contract (OpenAPI 3.0)

**Versioning:** Header-based versioning only. API paths are unversioned.

**JSON:API media type:** `application/vnd.api+json`

**NFR telemetry and health resources:**
- `GET /health`
- `GET /health/dependencies`
- `GET /observability/slo-status`

**Non-functional contract points:**
- All user-facing APIs must emit trace identifiers and structured error envelopes.
- Latency and error metrics must be tagged per operation and per organisation.
- Availability status endpoints must not expose sensitive internals while still providing operational diagnostics.

### Database Schema

**N/A — Non-Functional Requirements document.** REQ-015 specifies cross-cutting performance, availability, accessibility, and observability targets. No dedicated database table is owned by this requirement.

### Component Interfaces

```csharp
public interface INfrObservabilityService
{
  Task<Result<HealthStatusResource>> GetHealthAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
  Task<Result<DependencyHealthResource>> GetDependencyHealthAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
  Task<Result<SloStatusResource>> GetSloStatusAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}
```

### Alerting Conditions

| Condition | Threshold | Severity | Channel |
|---|---|---|---|
| p99 latency SLO breach (any user-facing API) | p99 > 2 seconds sustained for 5 min | HIGH | Ops alert |
| Availability SLO breach | Service availability < 99.9% over rolling 5-minute window | CRITICAL | On-call page |
| Accessibility regression | `jest-axe` violations detected in CI build | HIGH | CI build fail |
| Security header missing | `@emisgroup/acp-security-headers` check fails in deployment | CRITICAL | CI build fail |
| Cross-browser smoke test failure | Any browser environment fails baseline smoke tests | HIGH | CI build fail |

