## ✨ Evaluation Function Specification

### CHECK 1: NFR-001 — Performance Regression Test
- **Trigger:** CI pipeline / load test run
- **Test Scenario:** p99 latency under load
  - Setup: Simulate concurrent load at baseline throughput (per NFR-003)
  - Validation: p99 latency < 2 seconds for inbox load, search, document open, filing submission
  - Validation: No user-facing operation exceeds 2 seconds at p99 (except carved-out document viewer/conversion SLOs)
- **Pass Criteria:** p99 < 2 seconds confirmed under realistic load

### CHECK 2: NFR-002 — Availability Monitoring Active
- **Trigger:** Production deployment
- **Test Scenario:** Availability monitoring configuration
  - Validation 1: Uptime monitoring configured and active for all user-facing endpoints
  - Validation 2: Alert configured to trigger when projected 30-day availability falls below 99.95% (early warning before 99.9% breach)
  - Validation 3: RTO / RPO recovery procedures documented and tested
- **Pass Criteria:** Monitoring active; alert thresholds configured; recovery procedures tested

### CHECK 3: NFR-004 — Accessibility Automated Tests Pass
- **Trigger:** CI pipeline
- **Test Scenario:** jest-axe compliance
  - Validation 1: Every component test file includes `jest-axe` + `toHaveNoViolations()`
  - Validation 2: All automated accessibility tests pass with zero violations
  - Validation 3: No `@emisgroup/ui-*` components replaced with native HTML equivalents
- **Guardrail:** A11Y-010, DS-001
- **Pass Criteria:** Zero axe violations in CI; all components from EMIS-X design system

### CHECK 4: NFR-005 — Cross-Browser Smoke Tests Pass
- **Trigger:** Pre-release testing
- **Test Scenario:** Cross-browser compatibility
  - Validation: Core user journeys (inbox → file → code → task → done) tested and passing in Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari, and Electron
- **Pass Criteria:** No browser-specific failures in core journeys

### CHECK 5: NFR-006 — Security Headers Present
- **Trigger:** Any HTTP response from the application
- **Test Scenario:** Security header validation
  - Validation 1: `@emisgroup/acp-security-headers` security headers present in all responses
  - Validation 2: No hardcoded secrets detected in source code scan
  - Validation 3: TLS version ≥ 1.2 on all endpoints
- **Guardrail:** WSEC-013, SEC-001, SEC-002
- **Pass Criteria:** All security headers present; no secrets in code; TLS 1.2+ enforced

